# APEX-OS greeter — labwc environment (fallback host).
#
# labwc reads this file at startup and exports each KEY=value into the
# compositor + client environment.
#
# XKB_DEFAULT_LAYOUT is DELIBERATELY NOT SET HERE. It used to be pinned to
# `us`, which meant a QWERTZ/AZERTY user typed their password on the wrong
# layout at the one screen where that locks them out of the machine. Worse,
# a value set here would OVERRIDE the correct one: labwc applies this file on
# top of the inherited environment.
#
# The layout now arrives from the APEX keymap generator
# (/usr/lib/systemd/system-environment-generators/50-apex-keymap), which reads
# the system keymap from /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/00-keyboard.conf and exports
# XKB_DEFAULT_LAYOUT into greetd's environment; labwc inherits it. With no
# system keymap configured, nothing is exported and xkbcommon's own `us`
# default applies — identical to the old behaviour.

# No-GPU last resort (leave commented unless the target has no working GL —
# see README "No-GPU render fallback"; UNTESTED, real-HW verify item):
# WLR_RENDERER=pixman
# LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1
# QT_QUICK_BACKEND=software
